      "persona": "oncall.engineer",
      "seconds": 7.37,
      "answer": "New services on EKS should obtain their database credentials from Vault.  \nVault is the system of record for all application secrets on every cloud, and new services receive **dynamic database credentials from Vault** at the path `database/creds/<service>-rw` with a 1\u2011hour TTL, delivered by a Vault Agent sidecar (ADR\u20110027, reviewed 2026\u201105\u201107).  \nSecrets Manager is only used where an AWS service requires it (e.g., RDS Proxy) and is populated by Vault, not written by hand.",
