      "seconds": 7.86,
      "answer": "The quickest safe fix is to scale out the FNOL intake workers.  \nIf the workers are healthy but slow, increase the replica count up to the ceiling of 12 replicas (e.g., `kubectl -n fnol-prod scale deploy/fnol-intake-worker --replicas=12`).  \nIf the workers are crash\u2011looping, roll back to the previous stable deployment with `kubectl -n fnol-prod rollout undo deploy/fnol-intake-worker`.  \nNever purge the queue; the messages must be processed.  \nThese steps are documented in the \u201cFNOL intake queue backlog\u201d page (reviewed 2026\u201105\u201119).",
