      "seconds": 8.04,
      "answer": "The MQ\u2011to\u2011Kafka bridge triggers the `MqBridgeDepthHigh` alert when the `LPAS.POLICY.EVENTS.OUT` queue depth exceeds **50,000 messages for 15\u202fminutes** (or if no messages are committed to Kafka for 5\u202fminutes) (MQ\u2011to\u2011Kafka bridge lag, reviewed\u202f2026\u201107\u201128).  \nYou can run the bridge with up to **3 replicas**; scaling beyond that is not recommended because ordering per policy number relies on a single consumer per MQ queue partition (MQ\u2011to\u2011Kafka bridge lag, reviewed\u202f2026\u201107\u201128).",
