      "id": "gq-20",
      "trap": "none",
      "persona": "oncall.engineer",
      "seconds": 8.46,
      "answer": "LPB0420 abended with an S0C7 error overnight. According to the LPAS nightly batch abend documentation, Mainframe Operations is the first responder for any job abend, and the platform on\u2011call is only paged if a downstream AWS consumer is affected. The S0C7 error in LPB0420 is almost always caused by a bad packed\u2011decimal premium field; Operations will restart the job from STEP040 after moving the bad record to the suspense file LPAS.PROD.RENEW.SUSPENSE. Therefore, as platform on\u2011call you do not need to take action unless you see evidence that an AWS consumer (e.g., the billing run) is impacted. If the AWS consumer is not affected, simply monitor the job\u2019s restart and confirm the suspense file handling. (LPAS nightly batch abend, reviewed 2026-06-23)",
