      "answer": "The PCI tokenization KMS key is rotated every 180\u202fdays, or immediately if a compromise is suspected (Rotating the PCI tokenization KMS key, reviewed\u202f2026\u201104\u201121). Rotation is a dual\u2011control operation: two members of the `lm\u2011pci\u2011cde\u2011operators` team must be present\u2014one from Billing Engineering and one from Security Engineering (Rotating the PCI tokenization KMS key, reviewed\u202f2026\u201104\u201121). Each operator performs a distinct step: one creates the new key version, the other approves the alias switch, ensuring neither can complete the entire process alone.",
